Acrylic canvas.

1. The area around pages is painted with cairo_set_source_rgbi, which forces
   alpha to 1.0. Use the ARGB variant, and paint with CAIRO_OPERATOR_SOURCE so
   a translucent colour replaces the buffer instead of stacking on every
   repaint.
2. On screen only, paint the page background (paper colour and ruling) at
   reduced opacity. dontRenderEditingStroke is false only for the on-screen
   render path (RenderJob); previews, printing, image and PDF export all pass
   true and keep an opaque page.
3. Partial re-renders of the page buffer composite a freshly rendered
   rectangle over the old pixels; with translucent paper that stacks opacity
   (visible as darker rectangles). Replace the pixels instead, over exactly
   the mask's pixel-aligned extent: clearing the page-unit rectangle first
   leaves anti-aliased seams (hairlines) at fractional edges.

